# <project>/.claude/hpc.env — remote execution profile for hpc-submit.
# Developed-library paths live separately in .research-note/editables.env.

# --- remote HPC (optional; bootstrap --remote host:dir fills these) ---------
# The cluster runs jobs only — no Claude there. Project code reaches it through
# the project's Git origin; logs and small data come back via the
# fixer's rsync; the queue snapshot feeds the board and the J3/J4 lint.
# REMOTE_HOST is the DEFAULT host — the one used when an operation names no
# host (and, with REMOTE_HOSTS unset, the only host). REMOTE_DIR is its clone.
#REMOTE_HOST=hpc
#REMOTE_DIR=/path/to/project/clone/on/cluster
#REMOTE_DATA_MAX_MB=50
# Queue placement for this cluster — asked for at setup and applied by the
# submit step, so no submit file carries it. Leaving them unset means every job
# lands in whatever the cluster defaults to, which on a shared partition can be
# an hour of PENDING for a ten-minute job.
#REMOTE_PARTITION=<partition>
#REMOTE_RESERVATION=<group standing reservation, if you have one>
#REMOTE_ACCOUNT=<charge account, if the cluster requires one>

# Multi-remote (optional): declare EVERY cluster in REMOTE_HOSTS — no
# primary/secondary, all listed hosts are monitored equally (remote.sh queue
# and pull loop over the list; queue-snapshot rows are tagged `@<host>`).
# Each host's clone path lives in REMOTE_DIR_<host> (non-alphanumeric chars in
# the ssh alias map to `_` in the variable name); the default host may instead
# fall back to plain REMOTE_DIR. Leave REMOTE_HOSTS unset for the single-host
# contract above — it behaves exactly as before.
#REMOTE_HOSTS="hpc other"
#REMOTE_DIR_hpc=/path/to/project/clone/on/hpc
#REMOTE_DIR_other=/path/to/project/clone/on/other

# Machine-local overrides for this remote profile may go in
# .claude/hpc.local.env; keep that file out of Git.

# --- Julia (optional; unset = the project has no Julia environment) ---------
# The env directory this machine runs, repo-relative. `remote.sh push`
# instantiates it on the target host BEFORE checking it, so a far side that is
# merely behind is brought up rather than reported; doctor checks it here.
#JULIA_PROJECT=juliaenv
# A SECOND environment is allowed when one dependency exists on only one
# platform (MKL has no aarch64 build, so a shared file fails to instantiate on a
# Mac). It must STRICTLY CONTAIN the base — every package at the same version,
# plus its own extras — which is checked file-to-file in git, on every doctor run
# and on every push. Space-separated, repo-relative.
#JULIA_PROJECT_VARIANTS="juliaenv_gpu"
